cted symbol (e.g. _diff_links_inbound or _OUTBOUND_TO_INBOUND_FIELD) is moved to a sibling module and NOT re-exported into inbound_differ.py; the ~30 tests that do `inbound_differ.<symbol>` on the path-loaded module raise AttributeError even though `make lint` passes.","reconcile.py's `_load(...)` continues to load `inbound_differ.py` by filename, so the extracted sibling must itself be independently path-loadable (its own `_load(...)` or import must resolve under the same sys.path convention) or run_differs breaks at runtime."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a 'Consumers & re-export contract' subsection to the plan: (1) list the production loader path (reconcile.py `_load` by filename -> run_differs `inbound_differ_mod.<symbol>`) and note the extracted sibling must be independently path-loadable; (2) require re-importing every moved symbol back into inbound_differ.py with `# noqa: F401`; (3) require the string grep to specifically cover `inbound_differ._<private_symbol>` attribute forms across tests/, not only monkeypatch/getattr/importlib.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"l